/-!
# The two-rate onset current between the `++` and `−−` Laurent responses: assembly

By additivity of the current in both stream slots, the family, family/source, source/family and
source/source pieces assemble into the onset current between the complete scalar–scalar `++`
Laurent response at half-rate `s` (Laurent coefficients `A`, `B`) and the complete `−−` response at
half-rate `−3−s` (coefficients `A'`, `B'`), each with its harmonic sources
(`evenSector_skewOnset_SS`). The result `skewOnsetSS` is a single angular structure `P·Q` times an
explicit rational function; with the envelope `z^{−3}` of the two responses its radial integral is
the elementary part of the antisymmetrized `++−−` pairing.
-/

